  "verbalization": "Rubiyunnanin F is shown to have a target relationship with SNU-387, which is a compound that is a target of multiple pathways leading to prostate cells. These pathways include a complex molecule with multiple hydroxyl and carbonyl groups, and another compound, Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, which also targets prostate cells. The evidence suggests that Rubiyunnanin F may act through a mechanism that targets these compounds, which in turn affect prostate cells. The presence of multiple targets and their association with prostate cells implies a potential mechanism involving the inhibition of cellular processes critical to prostate function. The integrated evidence supports a relationship between Rubiyunnanin F and prostate cells through a pathway involving the targeting of SNU-387 and related compounds, which may interfere with cellular signaling or metabolic processes in prostate cells. The mechanism is not fully elucidated, but the observed targeting of these compounds to prostate cells suggests a possible role in prostate-specific functions.",
